SMS too.</p><form method="post"><input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="<?=h($_SESSION['csrf'])?>"><label for="notice-text">Message for configured recipients</label><textarea id="notice-text" name="notice_text" rows="2" maxlength="1000" required placeholder="Tea is ready. Please collect your tea."></textarea><label class="approval"><input type="checkbox" name="send_sms" value="1"> Also send to configured SMS recipients</label><button>Add notification</button></form><small>SMS is dispatched by the minute-by-minute scheduler. Editing or removing a notification cannot recall SMS already sent.</small><h3>Manage notifications</h3><?php foreach(publicNotices(true) as $n):?><form method="post" class="notice-editor"><input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="<?=h($_SESSION['csrf'])?>"><input type="hidden" name="notice_id" value="<?=$n['id']?>"><input type="hidden" name="notice_revision" value="<?=$n['revision']?>"><label>Notification · <?=date('d M H:i',$n['at'])?> EAT · <?=$n['at']<time()-3600?'Expired':'Visible on timer'?><textarea name="message" maxlength="1000" rows="2" required><?=h($n['message'])?></textarea></label><button name="notice_action" value="edit">Save notification</button> <button class="secondary" name="notice_action" value="remove" formnovalidate>Remove notification</button></form><?php endforeach?></section><section class="card simulator" id="simulator"><div class="eyebrow">PLAN BEFORE YOU CHANGE</div><h2>Give the day a little breathing room.</h2><p>Preview a delay against the current agenda. Protected breaks and closing times stay fixed unless you explicitly approve shifting them.</p><form method="post" id="adjustment"><input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="<?=h($_SESSION['csrf'])?>"><input type="hidden" name="command" value="EXTEND"><input type="hidden" name="revision" id="revision"><div class="form-grid"><label>Session<select name="id" id="session"><?php foreach($today as $r):?><option value="<?=$r['id']?>" data-revision="<?=$r['revision']?>"><?=h($r['title'])?></option><?php endforeach?></select></label><label>Adjustment (minutes)<input name="minutes" id="minutes" type="number" min="-240" max="240" value="15" required></label><label>Schedule policy<select name="policy" id="policy"><option value="protect">Protect breaks & closing time</option><option value="shift">Shift remaining sessions</option></select></label></div><button type="button" id="preview">Preview adjustment →</button><div id="simulation" aria-live="polite"></div><?php if($admin):?><label class="approval"><input type="checkbox" name="approved" value="1" required> I approve the revised timings and notifications to affected recipients.</label><button type="submit">Apply approved adjustment</button><?php else:?><small>Simulation only. Sign in to apply a revision.</small><?php endif?></form></section>
<section class="columns" id="report"><div class="card"><div class="section-label">PLANNED VS ACTUAL</div><h3>Every minute has a record.</h3><?php foreach(array_filter($today,fn($r)=>$r['actual_start']) as $r):?><p><b><?=h($r['title'])?></b><br>Started <?=date('H:i',$r['actual_start'])?> · <?=$r['actual_end']?($r['status']==='skipped'?'Skipped at ':'Ended ').date('H:i',$r['actual_end']).' · end variance '.round(($r['actual_end']-$r['original_end'])/60).' min':'Completion unconfirmed'?></p><?php endforeach?><p class="muted">Original timings are preserved. Actual times appear when organizers start and complete sessions.</p><?php foreach($logs as $log):?><small class="log"><?=date('d M H:i',$log['at'])?> · <?=h($log['action'])?></small><?php endforeach?></div><div class="card" id="connection"><div class="section-label">STAY IN THE LOOP</div><h3>From the room to your phone.</h3><p>Commands: ASK your question, STATUS, AGENDA, REPORT, START, NEXT, SWITCH session-id, DONE, PAUSE, RESUME, SKIP and EXTEND 15.</p><p>SMS reminders use Africa’s Talking with DairyOS’s server-side settings. WhatsApp can use a configured relay. Only approved organizer numbers can make changes; phone-based extensions use the protected policy.</p><span class="badge"><?=count(config()['recipients'])?> opted-in recipients</span><p class="muted">Only configured, opted-in recipients receive alerts. Provider acceptance and delivery are tracked separately.</p></div></section>
